course: dictionary
lesson: 6696
title: Occur: happen, be found, or come to mind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Occur is a formal word, so you will meet it in books and exams. It has three meanings. The first is to happen, often without being planned: «Mind it doesn't occur again!» means "don't let it happen again."
explain: The second meaning is to be found or to exist somewhere. «How many times does the number 3 occur?» asks how many times the number 3 appears. In science, earthquakes occur along faults, which means they happen in those places.
explain: The third meaning is occur to someone, which means an idea comes into their mind. «Selling the horse had not occurred to Toad before» means the idea had never come into Toad's mind. When you see occur with "to" and a person, read it as "came into their head."
fact: Occur means to happen, to be found, or to come into someone's mind.
fact: Occur is a formal word; in everyday talk, people often use happen instead.
fact: «It occurred to me» means the idea came into my mind.
fact: The forms are occur, occurs, occurred and occurring.
fact: Earthquakes occur along faults, which are cracks in the Earth's crust.
exercise: «Only later it occurred to her that she ought to have wondered at this.» What does occurred to her mean here? | It was found in her bag | *It came into her mind | It was planned by her | It made her angry
exercise: In maths, what does «how many times does the number 3 occur?» ask? | *How many times the number 3 appears | Who wrote the number 3 | Whether 3 is an odd number | How big the number 3 is
exercise: Toad is told, «Mind it doesn't occur again!» What does occur mean here? | To be found in a box | *To happen | To come into someone's mind | To be sold at a shop
test: «Selling the horse had not occurred to Toad before.» What does this tell us? | *The idea had never come into Toad's mind | Toad had sold the horse many times before | The horse was found in the woods | Toad was very happy about the horse
test: Earthquakes occur along faults. What does occur mean in this sentence? | *To happen, without being planned | To be sold to the highest bidder | To be cancelled for the day | To be felt only by animals
exam: Which sentence uses occur to mean come into someone's mind? | *It occurred to me that we could walk home | Mind it doesn't occur again | The number 3 occurs twice in this list | Earthquakes occur along faults
